From 7409ec52c594d77ea679e4724e1574ebc4b4ce2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NEMO Phase II executor <executor@nemo.local>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 00:52:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Phase II Rung 2: permanent ice gate + jac weight-plumbing
 on ice deposits

Codifies the ice-transport validation that was verified manually, and checks the
ice Jacobian on the toy BEFORE scaling (note 3).

- tests/coag_ice_gate.sh: runs the ice fixture with a monodisperse bin-1 start
  (constant kernel) and asserts, from abundances.out + dust_distribution.out:
    * gate (a) total ice sum_k Y(J_k X) conserved   -> 1.5e-15
    * dust-mass sum_k m_k n_k conserved (retained)  -> 3.5e-13
    * ice early-slope dY(J01X)/dt|_0 = -K0 nH Y(GRAIN01)_0 Y(J01X)_0 with the BARE
      K_11 (the 1/2 error would read ~2x)           -> 3.0e-6
- tests/jac_weight_check.sh now takes an optional input-dir argument (default
  inputs/, backward-compatible). Run on tests/fixture_ice_transport it exercises the
  grain + ice-transport product-weight plumbing into get_jacobian, including the
  catalyst product slot 6 the ice reactions add: 12 covered entries, 0 weight bugs,
  worst reldiff 2.9e-10. Ice abundance (1e-4) dominates grain (~1e-9), so the
  resolvable entries are the ice-transport ones. Default-network run unchanged
  (13450 entries, 1.8006e-3) -- coag-OFF still byte-identical.

Rung 2 core physics is now fully gated: conservation (a), dust-mass, ice rate,
eps!=0 split hand-check (b), and Jacobian weight plumbing. Remaining: ice-IC
machinery (area-weighted default + fractional override + coverage guard + round-trip
d) and scaling to the fiducial grid.
